The current Nocturne application shell is preserved byte-for-byte as app_legacy.js.
app.js is a compatibility bootstrap that loads app_legacy.js first, then the Nomad 2.x playback modules:
- playback-core.js: capability planning, playback sessions, Direct/HLS attachment, seeking and heartbeats
- track-control.js: embedded audio stream discovery/switching
- subtitle-control.js: embedded text subtitles via ticket-protected WebVTT, with legacy subtitle search preserved
- quality-control.js: Auto/Original/1080p/720p/480p session switching

This keeps the established UI intact while the new playback engine evolves independently.
